# Python bytecode / caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Scratch directories whose name starts with "plan", but **not** the plans
# themselves. This began as `plan*`, which matched every file and directory
# starting with those letters; the trailing slash narrowed it to directories.
#
# The leading slash is the second half of the fix: without an anchor the pattern
# also matched the `plans/` component inside `docs/plans/`, hiding the plan
# documents this project keeps under version control. Root anchoring keeps the
# root-level scratch directories out and lets `docs/plans/` in.
/plan*/

# Evaluation evidence under `eval/` is not a plan, it is evidence, and an
# evaluation that cannot be recomputed from the repository is not evidence.
# With the pattern above root-anchored this is already true; the negation is
# kept explicit so a future broad ignore rule does not silently hide it.
!eval/

# Virtual environments. `.venv-rl/` is the stage-G reinforcement-learning
# environment: about 4 GiB of CUDA wheels, regenerateable with one pip command.
.venv/
.venv-rl/
.venv-test/
venv/
env/

# `data/` is regenerable in principle and enormous in practice - the imitation
# shards, the H-B1/H-C2 datasets and every other training checkpoint - so it is
# ignored as a whole, which also covers `data/manifest.json`. Its contents are
# reproduced in `docs/reports/g_report.md`.
#
# The directory is grouped by learner lineage: `data/imitation/` holds the
# H-phase datasets and teachers, and `data/rl/{h,i,o,b,shared}/` holds each
# learner's training output. `data/README.md` maps every directory to its
# lineage and is the one file here that *is* tracked.
#
# **Except the six checkpoints the game can be played against.** A fresh clone
# has to be able to sit down and play, and a seat whose weights are not in the
# repository is not a seat - it is a name that fails to load on first use.
#
# The three lines per directory are not redundant. gitignore cannot re-include a
# file whose parent *directory* the pattern matched, so a single `data/*` plus
# `!data/imitation/hc2/step_001000.pt` below it is silently dead: `data/*` matches the
# directory `data/imitation/hc2`, and everything under an excluded directory stays
# excluded no matter what follows. The directory has to be un-ignored first,
# then its contents re-excluded, and only then can the one file be named.
#
# plan9a stage 4 published two of these four into `ai/checkpoints/` (verified
# sha256 against the source first), so their negations came out; plan9 task 4
# then retired all six imitation seats and put the 0k originals back under
# version control, which is what the four negations below do. `ai/checkpoints/`
# now holds only the four trained policies, so the only copy of the 0k weights
# that a fresh clone has is `data/` - and `data/` is where the retired-seat
# replays (`match.py --adhoc`) and `rl/`'s own tests read them from. Every one
# of the four was md5-checked against the `ai/checkpoints/` copy it replaces
# before that copy was deleted.
#
# `step_002000.pt` / `step_010000.pt` keep their negations for a different
# reason: those two were never published and are no longer a seat's load path
# either - they are simply the H-C2 weights the evidence cites, and deleting
# them was never on the table.
data/*
!data/README.md

# The lineage grouping added one level (`data/imitation/...` instead of
# `data/hc2`), so the parent directory has to be un-ignored before its own
# contents can be re-excluded - otherwise `data/*` matches `data/imitation` and
# no negation below can reach inside it. `!data/imitation/` + `data/imitation/*`
# is that un-ignore/re-ignore pair; the per-checkpoint negations follow.
!data/imitation/
data/imitation/*
!data/imitation/hc2/
data/imitation/hc2/*
!data/imitation/hc2/step_001000.pt
!data/imitation/hc2/step_002000.pt
!data/imitation/hc2/step_010000.pt
!data/imitation/imit_o1000/
data/imitation/imit_o1000/*
!data/imitation/imit_o1000/step_001000.pt
!data/imitation/imit_b1000/
data/imitation/imit_b1000/*
!data/imitation/imit_b1000/step_001000.pt
!data/imitation/imit_i1000/
data/imitation/imit_i1000/*
!data/imitation/imit_i1000/step_001000.pt

# No counterpart under `data/rl/`: every file there is ignored, so the old
# `!data/rl1/` + `data/rl1/*` pair had nothing to re-include and is gone.

# Runtime-generated game data (recreated on first play)
records.json
settings.json

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
